      "content": "**Why jobs can retry forever:**\n\nIn `worker.ts`, the retry logic is:\n\n```ts\nif (config.maxRetries === 0 || job.attempts < config.maxRetries) return enqueue(job);\n```\n\nThe condition `config.maxRetries === 0` short-circuits to `true`, so when `maxRetries` is `0`, the job is **always** re-enqueued regardless of how many attempts it has already made. The comment in the file confirms the intent: *\"maxRetries=0 explicitly means unlimited retries.\"*\n\nAnd in `config.json`, the value is set to:\n\n```json\n\"maxRetries\": 0\n```\n\nSo every failed job is re-enqueued indefinitely — there is no upper bound on attempts, and `deadLetter(job)` is never reached.\n\n**Correction:**\n\nChange `config.json` from:\n\n```json\n\"maxRetries\": 0\n```\n\nto:\n\n```json\n\"maxRetries\": 3\n```\n\nThis gives jobs a bounded number of retries (3), after which they are routed to the dead-letter queue instead of being re-enqueued forever.",
